### Characterisation

The unconstrained query overwhelmingly returns **`schema:Article`** entities (Wikidata sitelinks), because they are the first type encountered in the index ordering. Every `schema:Article` entity has exactly **5 outgoing triples** with a fixed property profile:

| Property | Value Pattern |
|---|---|
| `rdf:type` | Always `schema:Article` |
| `schema:about` | URI → a Wikidata entity (e.g., `wd:Q5296`) |
| `schema:inLanguage` | Language code literal (e.g., "aa") |
| `schema:isPartOf` | URI → the wiki site (e.g., `https://aa.wikipedia.org/`) |
| `schema:name` | Page title string literal |

These are **sitelink metadata nodes** — they represent Wikipedia/Wikimedia page entries that link back to Wikidata items. They are structurally simple (5 triples each) but extremely numerous (~99M instances), which is why they dominate the unconstrained sample.

